4 (e) In preparing the overall state budget for
5 distribution to the legislature, including any
6 supplemental, budget shortfall or other emergency changes
7 to the budget, the governor shall recommend to the
8 legislature that not less than five percent (5%) ten
9 percent (10%) of estimated general fund receipts for the
10 next biennial budget period shall be appropriated from the
11 general fund to the budget reserve account within the
12 earmarked fund. This appropriation shall be in addition to
13 any fund balance within the budget reserve account. At the
14 end of each biennial budget period, general fund
15 appropriations for the biennium in excess of expenditures
16 including encumbrances during the biennium, as identified
17 by the state auditor in accordance with the provisions of
18 W.S. 9-2-1008 and 9-4-207, shall be transferred into the
19 budget reserve account. All funds in the budget reserve
20 account shall be invested by the state treasurer and
21 earnings therefrom shall be credited into the general fund.
22 Appropriations to the account shall not lapse at the end of
2 HB0292

2025 STATE OF WYOMING 25LSO-0707
1 any fiscal period. Expenditures from the budget reserve
2 account shall be by legislative appropriation only.
3
4 9-2-1013. State budget; distribution of copies to
5 legislators; copies and reports of authorizations;
6 interfund loans.
7
8 (d) In addition to the items contained in subsection
9 (a) of this section and notwithstanding any other
10 recommendations made by the governor, the state budget
11 shall also include the governor's recommendations for
12 appropriations for the ensuing two (2) years, or if a
13 supplemental budget request, the remainder of the budget
14 period, subject to the following:
15
16 (ii) The total recommended appropriations under
17 this subsection for any two (2) fiscal year budget period
18 shall not exceed the total estimated revenues for that two
19 (2) year period. The total estimated revenues computed
20 under this paragraph shall not include increases in
21 existing revenue sources which would be available to the
22 state only after enactment of legislation in addition to
23 existing law, but shall include the unencumbered balances
